# --- The corpus ------------------------------------------------------------
# We deliberately do NOT commit the policy documents themselves.
#
# Two reasons:
#   1. Copyright. University policies are published publicly but are still
#      owned by the university. Committing a list of URLs is clearly fine;
#      re-publishing their PDFs is murkier.
#   2. It is better engineering. data/manifest.yaml plus the ingestion code
#      rebuilds the exact corpus from source, and the checksums prove you got
#      the same bytes. That beats a folder of binaries nobody can verify.
#
# data/manifest.yaml IS committed - it is the recipe. See the negation below.
data/raw/
data/processed/
data/index/
!data/manifest.yaml

# --- Python ----------------------------------------------------------------
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# --- Models ----------------------------------------------------------------
# Hugging Face caches downloaded models here. They are large and reproducible
# from the model names already recorded in config.yaml.
.cache/
models/

# --- Run logs --------------------------------------------------------------
# Individual run logs are local working data. Committed evaluation results go
# in eval/results/ as small summary files, so those are kept.
*.jsonl
!eval/adversarial.jsonl

# --- Editors and OS --------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# --- Secrets ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Nothing in this project needs a key today, since everything runs locally.
# This is here so that stays true by accident as well as on purpose.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.key
secrets.yaml
